course: dictionary
lesson: 308
title: Anarchist: one word, two meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: An anarchist is a person who believes there should be no government or rulers, and that people should organise themselves freely. Anarchist can also be an adjective, as in «anarchist ideas».
explain: Context tells you which meaning is used. «Nestor Makhno led an anarchist peasant army in southern Ukraine.» The clues are army and peasant, and the sentence adds that the army was against any government, so this is the first meaning.
explain: In everyday talk, some people use anarchist loosely to mean someone who wants to break rules and cause chaos. Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it right.
fact: An anarchist is someone who believes there should be no government or rulers.
fact: Anarchist can be a noun («an anarchist») or an adjective («anarchist ideas»).
fact: Anarchists had very different ideas; most were peaceful thinkers, and a few used violence.
fact: Loose use: anarchist can also mean someone who wants to break rules and cause chaos.
fact: «Nestor Makhno led an anarchist peasant army» shows an anarchist army fighting against any government.
exercise: What does an anarchist believe? | Every town should have a bigger police force | *There should be no government or rulers | Everyone should be ruled by one strong king
exercise: In «anarchist ideas», what kind of word is anarchist? | A noun | *An adjective | A full sentence | A verb
exercise: Jake says, «That boy is such an anarchist, he breaks every rule!» What does Jake mean by loose use? | A member of the school council | *Someone who wants to break rules and cause chaos | A peaceful thinker who writes books | Someone who sells old cars
test: Most anarchists were what kind of thinkers? | Royal | Violent | Rich | *Peaceful
test: In «Nestor Makhno led an anarchist peasant army», what kind of army was it? | A royal army guarding a palace | A navy at sea | A school band | *A peasant army fighting against any government
exam: Which sentence uses anarchist as a noun, meaning a person? | Ana wore an anarchist badge to school. | *Ana read about an anarchist who wrote about peaceful cities. | Ana read about anarchist ideas in a book.
